WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.600
Cold reduces battery chemical performance and can cause voltage sag under load.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.600
Usable endurance may be shorter than the displayed charge suggests,

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.650
especially during climb, acceleration, wind correction, or return.

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:13.930
Follow approved battery-temperature and preconditioning guidance.

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.970
Keep batteries within appropriate transport and staging conditions,

00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.860
confirm status before launch, and avoid improvised heating.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.870
Plan shorter flights and larger reserves in the cold.

00:00:22.870 --> 00:00:26.480
Heat stresses batteries, motors, electronics, mobile devices, and payloads.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.980
Direct sun, hot vehicles, repeated flights, hovering,

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.160
and processor load can raise temperatures beyond ambient conditions.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.990
Warnings, throttling, shutdown, or accelerated aging may follow.

00:00:35.990 --> 00:00:37.920
Storage and transport are part of weather management.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.255
Protect batteries from physical damage, extreme temperature, moisture,

00:00:41.255 --> 00:00:42.675
and conductive materials.

00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.010
Use approved charging, storage, inspection, and retirement practices.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:49.420
Monitor battery percentage, voltage or cell information when available,

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:52.855
temperature alerts, actual consumption, and unexpected changes.

00:00:52.855 --> 00:00:55.060
Compare outbound energy use with the return plan,

00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.320
especially when wind or payload load increases.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.540
Crew performance also changes in heat and cold.

00:00:59.540 --> 00:01:04.040
Gloves, glare, dehydration, fatigue, numb hands, and screen behavior can slow decisions,

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.635
so plan shelter, breaks, and shorter operating periods.

00:01:06.635 --> 00:01:09.520
Conservative reserve margins preserve options.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.760
If battery behavior differs from the plan, recover early.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:15.675
Do not use a successful warm-weather flight as evidence that the same route is safe in

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.095
cold,

00:01:16.095 --> 00:01:17.160
heat, or strong wind.
